/* Fixed Sliding Window */

=> Definition
A window of fixed length K moves across the array.

=> Example
Find maximum sum of 3 consecutive elements.
Array

2 1 5 1 3 2

K = 3
Possible windows
2 1 5 = 8

1 5 1 = 7

5 1 3 = 9

1 3 2 = 6
Answer
9

=> Brute Force
for every index

    calculate k elements
Time
O(n*k)

=> Optimized Sliding Window
Initial window
2 1 5

Sum = 8
Move window
Remove

2

Add

1

New Sum

7
Again
Remove

1

Add

3

New Sum

9
Again
Remove

5

Add

2

New Sum

6
No repeated calculation.

=> Algorithm
Compute first window sum.
Store answer.
Remove left element.
Add next element.
Update maximum.

=> Code
int maxSum(vector<int>& arr, int k){

    int n = arr.size();

    int windowSum = 0;

    for(int i=0;i<k;i++)
        windowSum += arr[i];

    int ans = windowSum;

    for(int i=k;i<n;i++){

        windowSum += arr[i];

        windowSum -= arr[i-k];

        ans = max(ans, windowSum);
    }

    return ans;
}

